1
00:04:56,470 --> 00:05:02,470
Love and imagination can change the world.

2
00:09:52,941 --> 00:09:58,941
Barbie as Rapunzel is a animation, family film directed by Owen Hurley.

3
00:14:49,411 --> 00:14:55,411
Barbie stars as Rapunzel, a young girl who is entrapped by
a magical barrier by the wicked, Gothel.

4
00:19:45,882 --> 00:19:51,882
Rapunzel finds an escape where she finds a Prince and a feud between two
kingdoms which goes back to the day she was kidnapped as a child.

5
00:24:42,352 --> 00:24:48,352
Barbie Roberts / Rapunzel (voice), played by Kelly Sheridan.

6
00:29:38,823 --> 00:29:44,823
Gothel (voice), played by Anjelica Huston.

7
00:34:35,294 --> 00:34:41,294
Penelope (voice), played by Cree Summer.

8
00:39:31,764 --> 00:39:37,764
Hobie / Palace Guard (voice), played by Ian James Corlett.

9
00:44:28,235 --> 00:44:34,235
Stefan (voice), played by Mark Hildreth.

10
00:49:24,705 --> 00:49:30,705
Hugo / General (voice), played by David Kaye.

11
00:54:21,176 --> 00:54:27,176
Barbie as Rapunzel is a 2002 animated fairy tale film co-produced by Mainframe
Entertainment and Mattel Entertainment, and distributed by Artisan Home Entertainment.

12
00:59:17,647 --> 00:59:23,647
An adaptation of the 1812 German fairy tale "Rapunzel" by the Brothers Grimm, it is the second
in the Barbie film series, with Kelly Sheridan providing the voice of Barbie.

13
01:04:14,117 --> 01:04:20,117
Barbie as Rapunzel was released on VHS and DVD on October 1, 2002, later
making a television premiere on Nickelodeon on November 24, 2002.

14
01:09:10,588 --> 01:09:16,588
and was subsequently released overseas through
Entertainment Rights and Universal Pictures Video.

15
01:14:07,058 --> 01:14:13,058
The film was nominated for eight DVD Premiere Awards, winning Best Original
Score and Best Animated Character Performance for Gothel.

16
01:19:03,529 --> 01:19:09,529
The film explores themes of princess, magic, based
on toy, female protagonist, dragon.
